# Color System — Virelle

Applies with `design/design-system.mdc`. Every color needs purpose, semantic role, and fit to the lingerie brand identity.

Do not introduce random HEX without a stated role. Prefer extending `src/styles/base/_variables.scss` for **both** ` :root` (dark) and `[data-theme="light"]`.

## Product context

| Cue | Direction |
|-----|-----------|
| Domain | Lingerie / sleepwear brand site |
| Tone | Soft luxury — intimate, elegant, calm |
| Neutrals | Charcoal (`#2b2b2b`) / near-black secondary; light theme soft white/gray |
| Brand metal | Gold `#d4af37` (`--color-gold`) — titles, highlights, premium edges |
| Atmosphere | Pink `#ffc0cb` / `#ffb6c1` — glass, borders, soft glow (not every surface) |
| Hero | Full-bleed photo + soft dark overlay gradient — not neon floods |

Gold is the **brand accent**; pink is **atmosphere**. Do not paint large chrome or every link pink.

## Architecture

### Surfaces

`--color-bg-primary` | `--color-bg-secondary` | `--color-bg-tertiary`

Section backgrounds may use `--gradient-bg-section`. Prefer tokenized surfaces over one-off fills.

### Text

`--color-text-primary` | `--secondary` | `--tertiary` | `--muted` | `--accent` | `--inverse`

Maintain contrast on both themes. Avoid pure `#000` page fills; dark page uses charcoal family already in tokens.

### Accents & feedback

- Gold: brand moments, hero name, carousel accents, premium borders
- Pink: glass panels, soft borders/shadows, hover atmosphere
- Overlays / modal / table tokens already exist — reuse them

```css
/* Bad */
color: #d4af37;
/* Good */
color: var(--color-gold);
```

### Glass / overlays

Use `--color-glass-*`, `--color-overlay-*`, modal/carousel tokens. Don’t invent competing blur stacks.

## Tokens in components

No scattered HEX in blocks when a variable exists. Theme-specific values belong under `:root` and `[data-theme="light"]` (or `.light-theme`).

## Palette changes

When proposing a palette change:

1. One-sentence brand direction
2. Map Gold (brand), Pink (atmosphere), Neutrals (surfaces/text), Semantic if needed
3. Provide dark **and** light remaps
4. Validate contrast (below)
5. Implement in `_variables.scss` first — then blocks

## Harmony

Restrained neutrals + gold + soft pink. Avoid neon backgrounds, rainbow UIs, purple-on-white SaaS defaults, glow spam that fights product photography.

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.2)

| Text | Minimum contrast |
|------|------------------|
| Normal | 4.5:1 |
| Large | 3:1 |

Focus-visible, clear hover/disabled. Never trade accessibility for style — especially gold-on-light and muted pink-on-dark.

## Themes

Not “white → black”. Separate semantic mapping. Gold stays; pink and text shift for readability. Never invert images/UI blindly.

## Output Format (new system / audit)

1. **Brand direction**
2. **Palette** — HEX + purpose
3. **Tokens** — CSS variable names matching project (`--color-*`)
4. **Dark / light** — both mappings

## Implementation Order

1. `_variables.scss` → 2. Blocks → 3. Contrast check → 4. States

For audits, follow `design/ui-review.mdc`.
